# Read the hand's current axis positions.
#
# PACKAGE-LOCAL contract, not a global one. The robonix source tree has no
# `robonix/primitive/hand/get_state`: the global hand set covers readback as the
# topic_out contracts `state_joint` / `state_finger`, whose IDL is
# `hand/msg/*.msg` — a codegen search root, not a buildable ROS package. Serving
# those would mean vendoring a copy of a global IDL and colcon-building it, i.e.
# owning a fork that drifts.
#
# The sibling package syswonder/primitive-linkerbot-linker_hand_o6-hand-rbnx
# reaches the same conclusion and exposes `get_state` instead — but ships no IDL
# for it, so that contract has nothing to generate from. This file is that
# missing IDL, so the contract is actually servable. Same id, same shape:
# on-demand axis-level readback.
---
# Request
# empty

# Response

# Whether the read succeeded.
bool ok

# Non-empty on failure: human-readable reason.
string message

# Current per-axis positions, [0,1] with 0=open / 1=closed. Axis names match
# those returned by the `info` contract.
JointValue[] joints
